WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.503
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedian you know from shows

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.037
such as "The Black Lady
Sketch Show"

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:06.106
and "Miracle Workers."

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:08.007
Her hit show "Abbott Elementary"

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:11.077
airs Tuesday nights on ABC.
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.746
-Recess is almost over.
-School is almost over.

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:15.381
-Okay, maybe if you guys
weren't double-handed.

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:16.649
Maybe it's not me.
Maybe it's you.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.218
Alright, here we go.

00:00:22.254 --> 00:00:23.656
Jacob, that was my turn.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.159
-♪ Down by the river
where the Green grass grows ♪

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.794
♪ There sat Janine,
sweet as a rose ♪

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:31.631
♪ Along came Jacob,
do a double-Dutch. ♪

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.265
♪ Janine's on the sidelines. ♪

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:36.202
♪ Jealous much? ♪

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.138
-Please welcome back
to the show,

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.839
our friend Quinta Brunson,
everybody.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.041
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:49.949 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:58.658 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:02.462 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.263
Welcome back, Quinta!
How you doing?

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:05.665
-Thank you for having me.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:06.966
-It is so lovely to have you.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.334
The first time you were on the
show with via Zoom,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.669
and now we have you
in New York City.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.337
Are you happy to be back
in New York?

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.438
-Mm-hmm.
-Okay.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.706
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.943
-It's so -- I know I've been
in New York before,

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.546
but I've been in L.A.
for 10 years now.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.547
-Yeah.
-And it's just --

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:24.550
there's trash everywhere
in New York.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.219
I just saw the prettiest lady
walk by a pile of trash,

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:30.089
and I was just like,
"What a way to live.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.657
What a way to live."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:33.292
Beautiful New York, yes.

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:36.896
-We have a very wide range
of experiences here.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.931
-You do. Yes, beautiful.
it's very nice.

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:40.366
I'm trying not to --
Come on, I just got my show.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.367
I don't want New Yorkers
to get mad.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.434
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:43.836
It's a very big chunk of people

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:44.937
that watch television.

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.372
You have a hit TV show --

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:49.809
a thing that is so hard to do,
especially a network comedy.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.777
It must be thrilling to have
come up with this idea

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.413
for a show and have people
respond to it.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:56.583
-It is. First of all,
it's kind of incredible,

00:01:56.583 --> 00:02:00.019
because I'm asking people
to tune in at a time

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:03.790
on a Tuesday night, and people
are actually tuning in to watch.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.259
And so, I have to say thank
you to people for doing that.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:09.261
It matters. It really matters.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.965
-And now you have people like
Scott over here

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.166
who want parts in the show.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.267
-Well, I support black
excellence, so...

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.770
-That's very nice to hear.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.639
-Wait, you told him that?

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.173
I telling him that now.

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:24.043
No, but that's so funny.
I did not know that.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.778
-Well, me and Tyler have been
talking about it.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:26.880
We'll talk about it.
We can have dinner.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.180
-Grabbing dinner after this.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.550
-That was very -- You're like,
"we'll talk later."

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:34.287
That's very L.A.
-You can come, too.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:37.890
-Scott and I were talking -- we
have parents who were teachers.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.525
Your mom was a teacher as well.
Kindergarten?

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.827
-Kindergarten teacher.
-And how does she feel?

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:43.062
Obviously, she must --
[ Applause ]

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.198
Yes, let's give it up
for all the teachers.

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:47.267
You obviously are writing
the show

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.001
based on experiences
you've had in school.

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:51.203
Does she respond to it?
Does she like what she sees?

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:52.404
-She loves it.

00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:55.741
She -- my mom is very...

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:57.142
Me being her daughter
doesn't matter.

00:02:57.142 --> 00:02:58.678
=She just enjoys the show,

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.580
and I think that's
the most positive

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.814
thing that I could
get out of it.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.282
She told me last week,
she's like,

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.717
"I'll watch this even
if you weren't on it."

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.619
And I was like,

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:10.056
"I don't know how I feel about
that," but she's enjoying it.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.792
There's some things that she
feels are directly taken

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.560
from her life, and they are --

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.029
like an episode
where the teacher,

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:19.932
Barbara Howard, doesn't remember
the student at all.

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:21.367
That's completely my mom.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:24.704
People come up to her all the
time, and she just pretends.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:27.172
She's so nice
and so sweet about it.

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:29.208
And then afterwards, she's like,
"I don't know who that boy was."

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:30.576
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.812
-Do you think she's convincing
to the boy in question?

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.980
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.350
If you saw your teacher walking
down the street and you went,

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.851
"Hey, Ms. Smith, Ms. Smith!"

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.653
And you believe
she remembers you, right?

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:44.256
Like she hasn't had seven Seths
since you've been in her class.

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:46.559
But, yeah, I mean,
she makes them believe it.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.627
She sells it.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.061
-So you obviously
are in show business,

00:03:49.061 --> 00:03:52.665
but you've gone back to your
mom's career of education.

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.500
But when you were in college...
-Yeah.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.669
-...you hosted a talk show.
-I did.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:04:00.573
-Now, was this on like
access television?

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.175
-It was on Facebook.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.009
-Okay, it was on Facebook.
-It was when Facebook

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:07.714
had just gotten videos,
so it wasn't what it is now.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.248
It was pure.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:12.951
It was like when you had to have
a college email address

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:15.288
to use it, and it was called
"The Rant."

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.757
And I just ranted about things
that happened on my campus.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.525
-Okay.
-And I had obscure guests.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.060
-Who were some of your guests?

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.395
-One of the guests
was just my friend.

00:04:23.395 --> 00:04:24.397
That's it.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.366
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:30.502
Another guest was this guy, Tim.

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:32.037
He was on because all
the Black girls thought he was

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:35.308
the hottest White guy on campus,
so that qualified him

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.842
being able to be
a guest on the show.

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:39.378
-And then, were the questions
about, "What is it about you,

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:41.380
that you think you're the
hottest White guy on campus?"

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.416
-No, and unlike you --
which is why I don't have

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.317
this kind of a show --
I just accosted him

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:46.986
with my own thoughts.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.921
And I don't think
I really asked him much.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.389
-Oh, you had a talk-at show.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:54.159
-Yeah, I did.
I did, I did, I did.

00:04:54.159 --> 00:04:55.827
-Philly, obviously,
is your home,

00:04:55.827 --> 00:04:58.598
and Philly is kind of having
having a moment, right?

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.432
-Yes, Philly is having a moment.

00:05:00.432 --> 00:05:02.768
They have "Abbott Elementary."
They have "Bel-Air."

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:04.937
We got James Harden.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.539
-You got James Harden.
-We got James Harden.

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.241
-James harden wanted --
-Why y'all hatin'?

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:10.476
Y'all don't...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.978
-James Harden was walking
down the street.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.613
He saw a beautiful woman
in garbage and he was like,

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.481
"I gotta get out there."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.882
He was like,
"I gotta force a trade."

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:20.119
-Gotta go, too.
Yeah, no, we're having a moment.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:22.621
It's really nice. I'm happy.
-And it must be nice.

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:26.959
Are people -- do you feel the
love from your home city?

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.161
-I feel it.
I feel it all the time.

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:30.662
It's nice to go back home.

00:05:30.662 --> 00:05:33.599
And I was just back there,
and I was just going

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:37.170
to the liquor store
to get -- get some liquor.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.738
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:42.508
That's what you get there,
and someone yelled at me,

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.377
"Ain't you Janine?"
And I was like, "I am."

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:45.777
And they were like, "Yeah, girl.

00:05:45.777 --> 00:05:46.912
You need to dump
that boyfriend."

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:48.213
And I was like, "Okay."

00:05:48.213 --> 00:05:50.649
Most people in Philly
just think the show is real.

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:53.252
Yeah, so...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.853
-Well, if they thought you were
an actor, they'd be like,

00:05:54.853 --> 00:05:56.188
"Why are you buying
your own liquor?"

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:58.958
-Yeah, it's very confusing
for them, the kids.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.794
Everybody's confused
about what's going on.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:06.332
-Alright. So, Scott is playing
a very believable --

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.901
in this new horror film --
adult film star.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:12.104
-Yeah.
-You had an early VO'er --

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:14.006
-Wait, wait, what?
Now, where's this going?

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:15.207
-Just watch.
-I know.

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:16.475
-Listen again.

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:18.077
Well, you won't believe how
good I am at transition.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.211
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.211 --> 00:06:20.947
You had a VO audition.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:22.448
-I did.
-Voiceover, sorry.

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:24.283
For the biz -- "VO,"
voice actor.

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:25.317
-Come on, Seth.

00:06:25.317 --> 00:06:27.286
-So, this is early
in your career.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:29.288
-You can't even call
it my career, at that point?

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:31.523
-Okay, got it.
-But I did.

00:06:31.523 --> 00:06:32.992
What's this come on, NBC?

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.760
My mom's not gonna -- I'll tell
her not to watch this show.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.896
But basically, the --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:38.564
-Can you just tell her
to watch the first part?

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:39.999
-Yeah, I know.
-I'd love her to get

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:41.300
a little face time.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.903
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Well, she likes the monologues.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.638
And then, I'll just tell her
the rest of it's canceled.

00:06:45.638 --> 00:06:46.872
That's what I tell her
when I don't want her

00:06:46.872 --> 00:06:47.907
to watch something.

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:50.009
I'm like,
"They canceled it, Mom."

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:52.745
So, I needed some money,
because I was really broke,

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.913
and I saw an opportunity
on Craigslist

00:06:54.913 --> 00:06:56.548
for some voiceover work.

00:06:56.548 --> 00:06:58.750
And I was like, "I want to be
in cartoons one day.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.452
I'd love to do that."

00:07:00.452 --> 00:07:02.655
So I click the link
and it's like,

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:04.424
"Play a character for someone

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:06.325
to call you up
and have a good time."

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:07.559
And I was like,
"That sounds fun."

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:08.895
-"Have a good time."

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:10.529
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.529 --> 00:07:13.165
-Cool, I'm gonna be a moose
with balloons for antlers.

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:14.499
-Yep.
-They're like, "No."

00:07:14.499 --> 00:07:17.470
-And they sent me my name,
and my name was Crystal.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.438
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.438 --> 00:07:23.608
And they sent me a picture of
who I was supposed to look like.

00:07:23.608 --> 00:07:25.444
I don't know if people know
who Buffie the Body is,

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:26.511
but that's who she --
You know Buffie the Body.

00:07:26.511 --> 00:07:28.714
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:32.184
-Very white audience,
but she's a very famous vixen.

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:34.386
She is really beautiful,
and they sent me a picture

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.622
of basically her,
and I had to, like,

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:40.559
pretend to be her on the
phone for people that called.

00:07:40.559 --> 00:07:42.361
-Yeah.
-And it was really gross.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:45.864
I couldn't get through it,
but they did tell the truth.

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:47.867
They said, "You will get paid
a dollar a minute,"

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:50.035
and I made $3 that day.

00:07:50.035 --> 00:07:51.604
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:53.972
I made $3.
-You know what?

00:07:53.972 --> 00:07:55.241
When people are up front,

00:07:55.241 --> 00:07:57.209
you have to give them
respect for that.

00:07:57.209 --> 00:07:59.278
Alright, well, congratulations
on season 2.

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:01.180
-Thank you.
-I hope, over dinner tonight,

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.514
Scott talks his way into it.

00:08:02.514 --> 00:08:03.615
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:08:03.615 --> 00:08:04.883
-He's Kid Cudi.
It's pretty easy.

00:08:04.883 --> 00:08:07.319
I don't know why he's like --

00:08:07.319 --> 00:08:09.054
Tyler was like, "This guy wants
to be on the show."

00:08:09.054 --> 00:08:11.490
I was like, "Yeah, he can."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.459
-You guys,
that's Quinta Brunson.

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:16.762
"Abbott Elementary" airs
Tuesday nights on ABC.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:18.231
Kid Cudi over there.
We'll be right back.

